## Character-level tiny GPT

[Tutorial_Understand_a_Tiny_GPT.ipynb](Tutorial_Understand_a_Tiny_GPT.ipynb) trains a small decoder-only Transformer in PyTorch on a public-domain Shakespeare subset, then inspects the causal mask, position embeddings, context length, and sampling temperature.

Open in Colab on the review branch `cursor/tiny-gpt-character-tutorial-9992`. That link works before the pull request merges. The `main` link does not open this notebook until then.

- Review branch: https://colab.research.google.com/github/thinkinginmath/ML-tutorials/blob/cursor/tiny-gpt-character-tutorial-9992/Tutorial_Understand_a_Tiny_GPT.ipynb
- After merge: https://colab.research.google.com/github/thinkinginmath/ML-tutorials/blob/main/Tutorial_Understand_a_Tiny_GPT.ipynb

The notebook text is [CC BY-NC-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/). The Shakespeare subset is downloaded at runtime and is not stored in this repository.

```bash
python -m unittest tests.test_tiny_gpt_notebook_smoke
```

Leave `TINY_GPT_TRAIN_STEPS` unset for the default lesson. `TINY_GPT_LONG=1` trains longer. A value of `2` only checks that the code path runs; do not quote those losses.
